# Monthly btrfs scrub - the OpenRC/cron equivalent of btrfs-scrub.timer on the
# systemd machines. Scrub reads every block and checks it against its stored
# checksum; on a single-device filesystem it detects corruption and names the
# file but cannot repair data, which is still worth knowing while backups are
# fresh rather than a year later.
#
# First Sunday of the month at 00:15. Output goes to syslog via cron, which is
# why metalog had to be running before this was worth adding.
15 0 1-7 * 0  root  /usr/local/sbin/fd44-btrfs-scrub
